From 631d2f70bc637021e966829433e028f8be4c31ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Verbovoy <ivanverbovoy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 23:54:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] sfduo-control: org.sfduo.Phoc.Tile puts an app's windows on a
 half, sliding

The port's dock moved a window to the other half as a user would: focus,
wait, the tiling chord - half a second a window, and two windows of a pair
were raised in turn and jumped one after the other. Tile(app_id, side) on
the session bus tiles an app's windows directly: nothing is focused or
raised, and each window's last buffer slides from where it was to where it
goes (a MOVE ghost, 260 ms) while the window itself is hidden, then shown.
---
